1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
If your wipers are smearing instead
of clearing, that's not just rain.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Cracked, hardened rubber can't hold
an edge — it drags instead of wiping clean.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Chattering or skipping across dry glass
is often that same worn edge.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Most shops say six months to a year,
but heat and UV wear rubber faster.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
One clue: a hairline crack, or a rough,
glazed edge instead of a clean line —

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
worth checking before the next storm.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look.
